#: passwords.cpp:40
msgid "Echo Characters As"
msgstr "Teken wiesen as"

#: passwords.cpp:42
msgid ""
"You can select the type of visual feedback given when you enter a password in "
"kdesu. Choose one of the following options:<p> <ul><li><em>1 star:</em> "
"each character you type is shown as an asterisk (*) symbol.</li> <li><em>"
"3 stars:</em> three asterisks are shown for each character you type.</li> <li>"
"<em>no echo:</em> there is no visual feedback at all, so nothing on your screen "
"shows how many characters are in your password.</li></ul>"
msgstr ""
"In kdesu kann man utsöken, as wat de Teken wiest warrt, wenn en Passwoort "
"ingeven warrt. Söök een vun disse Optschonen ut:<p> <ul><li><em>1 Steern:</em> "
"elk Bookstaav, den man ingifft, warrt as'n 'Asterisk' (=*) wiest.</li> <li><em>"
"3 Steerns:</em> dree Asterisken warrt för elk Bookstaav wiest.</li> <li><em>"
"Keen Teken:</em> dor warrt överhööft keen Teken wiest, also wiest nix op'n "
"Schirm, woveel Teken in dat Passwoort sünd.</li></ul>"

#: passwords.cpp:49
msgid "&1 star"
msgstr "&1 Steern"

#: passwords.cpp:50
msgid "&3 stars"
msgstr "&3 Steerns"

#: passwords.cpp:51
msgid "&No echo"
msgstr "&Keen Teken"

#: passwords.cpp:56
msgid "&Remember passwords"
msgstr "&Passwöör behollen"

#: passwords.cpp:57
msgid ""
"If this option is checked, kdesu will remember your passwords for the specified "
"amount of time. Until then, you will not have to enter your password again. "
"Keep in mind that this option is insecure and may enable others to damage your "
"system.<p> Please <em>do not</em> use this option if you are working in an "
"insecure environment, for example, on a workstation that is located in a "
"publicly accessible area.<p> This option does not affect passwords explicitly "
"set in other applications, for example, your email account password in KMail."
msgstr ""
"Wenn disse Optschoon utsöcht is, warrt kdesu dat Passwoort för de fastsett Tiet "
"behollen. Bet dorhen bruukt dat Passwoort nich nochmaal ingeven warrn. Aver "
"mark op: Disse Optschoon is nich seker; se lett to, dat anner Lüüd op dat "
"Systeem un de Daten togriepen.<p> Bitte <em>bruuk disse Optschoon nich</em>"
", wenn du in'n unseker Ümgeven arbeidst, t.B. op'n Reekner, op den faken "
"verscheden Lüüd arbeidt.<p> Disse Optschoon hett keen Inwarken op Passwöör, de "
"in anner Programmen sett worrn sünd, t.B. dat Passwoort för't Nettpost-Konto in "
"KMail."

#: passwords.cpp:70
msgid ""
"You can specify how long kdesu will remember your passwords. A short timeout is "
"more secure than a long timeout."
msgstr ""
"Man kann utsöken, wo lang kdesu dat Passwoort behollen schall. En korte Tiet is "
"sekerer as'n lang."

#: passwords.cpp:73
msgid "&Timeout:"
msgstr "&Tiet:"

#: passwords.cpp:76
msgid " min"
msgstr " Min"

#: passwords.cpp:189
msgid ""
"<h1>Passwords</h1> This module gives you options for configuring the way in "
"which the \"kdesu\" program treats passwords. Kdesu will ask you for a password "
"when you try to carry out some privileged actions, such as changing the "
"date/time stored in your system clock, or adding new users on your computer.<p> "
"You can configure the type of visual feedback given when you type a password, "
"and whether kdesu should remember passwords for some time after you have given "
"them.<p> Note that these settings affect <em>only</em> "
"kdesu. This means that the behavior of passwords in KMail and other programs "
"cannot be configured here."
msgstr ""
"<h1>Passwöör</h1> Mit Hülp vun dit Moduul kann de Metood instellt warrn, de "
"\"kdesu\" för't Behanneln vun Passwöör bruukt. Kdesu warrt na'n Passwoort "
"fragen, wenn priviligeert Aktschonen utföhrt warrn schallen, as t.B. de "
"Systeemtiet ännern oder niege Brukers op den Reekner inrichten.<p> "
"Man kann instellen, wodennig Bookstaven wiest warrt, wenn man'n Passwoort "
"ingifft, un wat kdesu achterna dat Passwoort en Tiet lang behollen schall.<p> "
"Aver mark op, dat disse Instellen <em>bloots</em> kdesu bedrapen. Dat bedüüdt, "
"dat dat Verhollen vun Passwöör in KMail oder in annere Programmen hier nich "
"instellt warrn kann."

